 "sarvam_vocals": {
  "text": "Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line. Common to everything in the universe motion motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run, sleeping. Air moves into and out of our lungs, blood flows in arteries, veins. Carry people, automobiles, and planes. Water flowing down a dam, leaves falling from trees. Earth rotates once every 24 hours, revolves round the sun. Once in a year, the sun in motion in the Milky Way, Milky Way, moving within its local group of galaxies. Rectilinear motion, uniform acceleration, a set of simple equations, relative nature of motion, relative velocity. Point objects valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations, size neglected without much error. Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line. ",
